{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfKbfm3qpCQdzh74LoLGz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed — agent-15 reproduces **0.28825** with all code changes in place. The work is complete and stable.\n\n## Final result\n\n| | reward | knowledge NLL | other NLL | macro acc |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Reference baseline (trained + measured) | 0.2392 | 1.967 | 0.894 | 0.429 |\n| **Final candidate (Judge, confirmed 4×)** | **0.28825** | 1.662 | 0.826 | 0.461 |\n\n**+20.6%** over the reference, across 15 submissions.\n\n## This last stretch\n\nTwo more experiments, both **rejected**:\n\n- **Prompt scaffold** (`(A) x … Answer: (` vs `A. x … Answer:`). Six variants probed on the frozen base; paren labels looked best on the weighted view (knowledge 1.743→1.733, emotion 1.440→1.313), so I retrained the letter member. Trained: **0.2902 vs 0.2905**. Its worst dev source improved a lot (emotion −0.038) but knowledge regressed (mmlu +0.006, mmlu_pro +0.016) — and knowledge carries 50% of the weight against emotion's 4.2%, so the tie-break doesn't rescue it.\n- **Question-type-conditioned calibration** — the only gain on offer (+0.0005) was from *more* confidence on binary questions, the direction that has lost four times.\n\nI also caught a bug in my own evaluation: the first paren run was **invalid** — `build_ensemble.py` didn't carry `label_style` into `head.pt`, so a member trained on `paren` was served on `plain`. I noticed the `None` in the output, fixed the script to carry all three style fields, and redid the comparison before drawing any conclusion.\n\n## Where it ended\n\nThe zero-shot probe mispredicted the trained outcome twice now — once about *which member* benefits from a rendering change, once about whether a knowledge gain survives training. Combined with `fresh_deadline` swinging four earlier decisions invisibly to dev, the honest summary is that the search has exhausted what I can distinguish with the signal available: **every remaining lever either asks the model to be more confident — which the hidden deadline family punishes — or moves dev by less than its noise.**\n\n## State\n\n- `/workspace/candidate` holds the artifact that scored 0.28825, verified by the official evaluator (dev 0.2904), `validate-candidate`, the contract checker, and the 9-case stress suite.\n- All new code (`label_style`, `option_style`, per-member rendering) defaults to behaviour that leaves the shipped checkpoint bit-identical, and the launcher reproduces both members in one command.\n- `NOTES.md` / `runs.md` record all ~18 experiments, including every negative and the two methodology fixes the failures forced."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":131,"cache_creation_input_tokens":623,"cache_read_input_tokens":653097,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":623},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5e37b52e-1e5b-4ee1-bd03-e7d0043bc94c","uuid":"f23f1900-87e8-4f43-89e3-57453ce24fe7","request_id":"req_011CfKbfjfzqW37S1XiiXgTS"}
