{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfKfK7HdoV1rq7rUj8fgu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017t2fjaE9GDYEa5qZAH1PdY","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> runs.md <<'EOF'\n\n### Re-tuning after the serving change: already optimal\nChanging the serving rendering could have moved the calibration optimum, so the full grid was\nre-run on a fresh cache. Unconstrained, the best is 0.2938 (order-averaging the letter member as\nwell) — but it costs emotion +0.052, sciq +0.031, paws +0.014, the familiar shape of a change that\nbuys the mean with the worst source.\n\nConstrained so that **no** development source may regress by more than 0.002, the best reachable\nis 0.2925 against the shipped 0.2924, out of 13 qualifying settings. The shipped calibration\n(w 0.45, power 0.7, floor 0.01, beta 1.0, orders 1/2) is already at that constrained optimum.\nNo change made.\n\n### Harness bug, third instance — and the fix that ends the class\n`sweep_ensemble.py` keyed its member cache on the checkpoint *directory name*, so re-running it\nafter changing weights or serving styles silently reused a stale file. This produced a re-tune\nagainst a seven-hour-old cache that reported dev 0.2863 for a configuration the evaluator scores\nat 0.2924 — a plausible number, wrong. Together with the two `build_ensemble.py` drifts, three\ncomparisons in this session were invalidated by a harness detail rather than by the model.\n\nFixes: `build_ensemble.py` now delegates to the shipped `kev.ensemble.assemble` instead of\nduplicating it, and the member cache key now includes a SHA-256 digest [REDACTED] `head.pt`, so a cache\nwritten for different weights or styles cannot be reused. Every number above was re-derived after\nthese fixes. The lesson generalises: a silent wrong number is worse than a crash, and an\nevaluation harness needs the same \"can this be stale or mismatched?\" scrutiny as the model.\nEOF\n/opt/kev-venv/bin/python -c \"\nimport torch;h=torch.load('/workspace/candidate/checkpoint/head.pt',map_location='cpu',weights_only=True)\nprint('candidate:', h['letter_style'], h['pointer_style'], {k:h[k] for k in ('weight','prob_power','p_floor','beta_member','orders_letter','orders_pointer')})\"\nvalidate-candidate --json | head -2\nCUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 /opt/kev-venv/bin/python check_contract.py /workspace/candidate/checkpoint 2>&1 | grep -E '\"(parameters|projected|peak_gib|max_sibling_delta|max_history_delta|status)\"'\nCUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 /opt/kev-venv/bin/python stress.py 2>&1 | tail -2","description":"Record findings and run the final verification chain","timeout":2400000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1855,"cache_read_input_tokens":687444,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1855},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5e37b52e-1e5b-4ee1-bd03-e7d0043bc94c","uuid":"716f8587-91d0-4a83-895b-186a11f3255c","request_id":"req_011CfKfK6cTTJafV7xUH9wyS"}
