{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfKfoAPhagUMSLLvK7qEZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed — the workspace reproduces **0.28955** with all fixes in place.\n\n## Final result\n\n| | reward | knowledge NLL | other NLL |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Reference baseline (trained + measured) | 0.2392 | 1.967 | 0.894 |\n| **Final candidate (Judge, confirmed 2×)** | **0.28955** | 1.661 | 0.818 |\n\n**+21.1%** over the reference, across 17 submissions.\n\n## This round\n\n**Re-tuned the calibration** after the serving-rendering change, since that could have moved the optimum. Unconstrained, dev offers +0.0014 (order-averaging the letter member) — but at the cost of emotion +0.052, sciq +0.031, paws +0.014: the exact shape that has lost on the Judge every time. Constrained so no dev source may regress by more than 0.002, the best reachable is 0.2925 against the shipped 0.2924. **The shipped calibration is already at the constrained optimum**, so no change.\n\n## The third harness bug — and the fix that ends the class\n\n`sweep_ensemble.py` keyed its member cache on the checkpoint *directory name*, so re-running it after changing weights or serving styles silently reused a stale file. My re-tune ran against a **seven-hour-old cache** and reported dev 0.2863 for a configuration the evaluator scores at 0.2924. I caught it only because that number contradicted the evaluator — a plausible wrong number, not a crash.\n\nThat's the third comparison this session invalidated by a harness detail rather than by the model (the other two were `build_ensemble.py` silently dropping `label_style` and `cloze_views`). Both root causes are now closed:\n\n- `build_ensemble.py` **delegates** to the shipped `kev.ensemble.assemble` instead of duplicating it, so experiments can't drift from what the launcher writes.\n- The member cache key now includes a **SHA-256 digest [REDACTED] `head.pt`** — a cache written for different weights or styles cannot be reused.\n\nEvery number in `runs.md` was re-derived after these fixes, and the fresh cache now agrees with the official evaluator to the fourth decimal.\n\nThe generalisable lesson, which I've written up: **a silent wrong number is worse than a crash**, and the evaluation harness deserves the same \"can this be stale or mismatched?\" scrutiny as the model. All three bugs produced results that looked entirely reasonable; two of them would have led me to discard genuinely good work, and the third nearly sent me re-tuning against noise.\n\nFinal state verified: `validate-candidate` clean, 1.3e-6 sibling sensitivity, 0 history sensitivity, 512.5M params, 2.05 GiB peak, stress suite passing. Archived at `experiments/best_0.28955`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":260,"cache_read_input_tokens":690789,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":260},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5e37b52e-1e5b-4ee1-bd03-e7d0043bc94c","uuid":"9dd65fe3-f6df-419c-9563-5e47e7dcfd72","request_id":"req_011CfKfo9EVxwChqUffDNpvi"}
