{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfKg8LJYXNSxT5CkU55SA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YVzrGmfhCmctdmiTvaRtPJ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> runs.md <<'EOF'\n\n### Label style at serving: must match training (unlike the option key)\nServing the `plain`-trained members with `paren` labels: dev 0.2894 against 0.2924, worse on both\ngroups (knowledge +0.014, other +0.007) and on the worst source (emotion +0.049).\n\nThe contrast with the option-key result is the point. The **label markup is structural** — the\nhead's letter view reads one specific vocabulary row (\" A\"), and its learned option-slot prior is\nindexed to it — so changing it at serving time breaks a channel the head depends on. The\n**option key is additive content** inside a span the head already reads through its lexical view,\nso handing it over at serving time enriches rather than breaks. Serving-time input can carry more\ninformation than training, but not different *structure*.\nEOF\ncd /workspace/candidate && python - <<'PY'\nimport pathlib\np=pathlib.Path('kev/decision.py'); s=p.read_text()\ns = s.replace('def encode(tok, rec, max_state=MAX_STATE, max_branch=MAX_BRANCH, strict=False, label_style=\"plain\"):',\n              'def encode(tok, rec, max_state=MAX_STATE, max_branch=MAX_BRANCH, strict=False, label_style=\"plain\",\\n           restate=False):')\ns = s.replace('''        branch += tail\n        base = len(ids)''',\n'''        if restate:\n            # Additive, serving-time only: put the instruction back in front of the answer cue.\n            # With ten long options the cue can sit hundreds of tokens from the question.\n            branch += tok(\"\\\\n\" + safe(question[\"instr\"]), add_special_tokens=False).input_ids\n        branch += tail\n        base = len(ids)''')\ns = s.replace('''    def encode(self, tok, rec, **kw):\n        return encode(tok, rec, label_style=self.label_style, **kw)''',\n'''    def encode(self, tok, rec, **kw):\n        return encode(tok, rec, label_style=self.label_style, restate=self.restate, **kw)''')\ns = s.replace('        self.cloze_views = False', '        self.cloze_views = False\\n        self.restate = False')\np.write_text(s)\np=pathlib.Path('entrypoint.py'); s=p.read_text()\ns = s.replace('    model.letter_style = meta.get(\"letter_style\", model.letter_style)',\n              '    model.letter.restate = bool(meta.get(\"restate\"))\\n    model.letter_style = meta.get(\"letter_style\", model.letter_style)')\np.write_text(s); print(\"ok\")\nPY\n/opt/kev-venv/bin/python -c \"import ast;[ast.parse(open(f).read()) for f in ('kev/decision.py','entrypoint.py')];print('parses')\"\nfor rs in 0 1; do\n/opt/kev-venv/bin/python - \"$rs\" <<'EOF'\nimport torch, os, sys\np=\"/workspace/experiments/ens_dsc/head.pt\"; h=torch.load(p,map_location=\"cpu\",weights_only=True)\nh.update(label_style=\"plain\", restate=bool(int(sys.argv[1])), letter_style=\"key_desc\", pointer_style=\"key_desc\",\n         weight=0.45, prob_power=0.7, p_floor=0.01, orders_letter=1, orders_pointer=2, beta_member=1.0)\ntorch.save(h,p); os.chmod(p,0o644)\nEOF\nprintf \"restate_instruction=%s -> \" \"$rs\"\nCUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 /opt/kev-venv/bin/python evalrun.py /workspace/experiments/ens_dsc --tag rs_$rs 2>/dev/null | head -1 | sed 's/.*reward=/dev reward=/'\ndone","description":"Test restating the instruction before the answer cue","timeout":2400000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1668,"cache_read_input_tokens":692016,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1668},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5e37b52e-1e5b-4ee1-bd03-e7d0043bc94c","uuid":"8e033c6e-8bae-4018