{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfKh8Re8NAu2TnWJZf9tv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed at **0.28955** (18 submissions). The serving-time axis is now fully mapped and the work is stable.\n\n## Final result\n\n| | reward | knowledge NLL | other NLL |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Reference baseline (trained + measured) | 0.2392 | 1.967 | 0.894 |\n| **Final candidate (Judge)** | **0.28955** | 1.661 | 0.818 |\n\n**+21.1%** over the reference.\n\n## This round: closing out the axis a bug opened\n\nThe biggest late gain came from a mistake — a drifted assembler served members trained on `desc` with the upstream `key: desc` rendering, and that \"broken\" configuration was better. Rather than just bank it, I probed where the boundary is, using pure head-buffer flips (no retraining):\n\n| serving-time change | dev | verdict |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| restore the criteria key inside each option | 0.2924 | **kept** (Judge +0.0013) |\n| `paren` labels instead of `plain` | 0.2894 | rejected |\n| restate the instruction before the answer cue | 0.2911 | rejected |\n\nOne rule explains all three: **additive content inside a span the head already reads helps; changing structure, or adding tokens in positions the head never saw, hurts.** The key lands inside the option span the lexical view reads. The label markup *is* the letter view's addressing. A restated instruction is new material the head has no use for.\n\nThat's a real, transferable finding — serving input need not match training input, but only additively — and the asymmetry is the whole effect (training *and* serving with keys is worse than either).\n\n## A fourth silent failure, this one mine\n\nMy `restate` test printed nothing because I ran it from the wrong directory with `2>/dev/null`. It looked like an empty result rather than an error. That's the fourth silent-failure instance this session — three from harness drift, one from my own command. I've stopped suppressing stderr, and the two structural fixes (delegating to the shipped assembler; digest-keyed caches) are what actually prevent recurrence.\n\n## State\n\n`/workspace/candidate` holds the 0.28955 artifact, unchanged by any of this round's probes — verified: `validate-candidate` clean, 512.5M params, 2.05 GiB peak, 1.3e-6 sibling sensitivity, 0 history sensitivity, stress suite passing. Archived at `experiments/best_0.28955`; 621 lines of notes covering ~24 experiments, every negative result, and both harness bug classes with their fixes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":897,"cache_read_input_tokens":698917,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":897},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5e37b52e-1e5b-4ee1-bd03-e7d0043bc94c","uuid":"1bd95e10-4d01-4d38-b4e1-11e09b8ec8c4","request_id":"req_011CfKh8QzBdFSN2FFJanMY5"}
