{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfKhYF2KMLb2kgnztbRdg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015Fpjmnxcr1Zo2839Hn3oF9","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> runs.md <<'EOF'\n\n### Indexed ordinal options: a fix for a real defect that the head cannot use\nThe head's lexical view reads each option's first token, and ordinal level descriptions routinely\nshare one — \"very negative\"/\"very positive\", \"Covered in full\"/\"Covered at half cost\". **94% of\nthe fixed corpus's 3,448 ordinal questions collide** (25% of development's), so that view is blind\non them. Prefixing the level index makes every first token [REDACTED] dev 0.2923 against 0.2924 — neutral, with `unknowable_control` +0.008. Accuracy rose\n(0.4671 -> 0.4737) but NLL did not.\n\nThe explanation refines the serving-enrichment rule. Because 94% of ordinal training questions\ncollided, the head *learned that the lexical view is useless for this question type* and routes\naround it; the view gates are shared across types, so there is no mechanism by which handing it a\nusable token [REDACTED] inference makes it trusted again. Enrichment pays only where the head already\nrelies on the channel being enriched — which was true of Choice options and their keys, and is\nnot true of ordinal options.\n\nFixing this properly would mean training with indexed levels, not serving with them. It is left\nundone deliberately: the win would land on the ordinal share of the policy families, and the\nevidence needed to justify another full retrain is not there.\nEOF\n/opt/kev-venv/bin/python -c \"\nimport torch;h=torch.load('/workspace/candidate/checkpoint/head.pt',map_location='cpu',weights_only=True)\nprint('candidate:', h['letter_style'], h['pointer_style'], '| score_style=', h.get('score_style','(absent->plain)'))\"\nvalidate-candidate --json | head -2\n/opt/kev-venv/bin/python /opt/kev-runtime/evaluate_public.py --candidate /workspace/candidate 2>&1 | grep -v Warning | /opt/kev-venv/bin/python -c \"\nimport json,sys; print('candidate dev=%.4f (Judge 0.28955)'%json.load(sys.stdin)['metrics']['reward'])\"","description":"Record the ordinal finding and verify the candidate","timeout":2400000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1375,"cache_read_input_tokens":705447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1375},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5e37b52e-1e5b-4ee1-bd03-e7d0043bc94c","uuid":"39db3c9b-45af-47fb-95c5-ecf590054010","request_id":"req_011CfKhYDiSWaFDFou4kieyP"}
