{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfKiLQKhYhr59JmV4kf1F","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed at **0.28955** (19 submissions), workspace stable.\n\n## Final result\n\n| | reward | knowledge NLL | other NLL |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Reference baseline (trained + measured) | 0.2392 | 1.967 | 0.894 |\n| **Final candidate (Judge)** | **0.28955** | 1.661 | 0.818 |\n\n**+21.1%** over the reference.\n\n## This round: testing a defect that looked eminently fixable\n\nThe serving-enrichment rule I'd just derived predicted a win here, and it was wrong — which made it the most informative test of the round.\n\nThe head's lexical view reads each option's **first token**. Ordinal level descriptions routinely share one (`\"very negative\"`/`\"very positive\"`, `\"Covered in full\"`/`\"Covered at half cost\"`) — I measured that **94% of the fixed corpus's 3,448 ordinal questions collide**, so that view is blind on them. Prefixing the level index makes every first token [REDACTED] additive content, in exactly the span the head reads.\n\nIt changed nothing (dev 0.2923 vs 0.2924; accuracy rose 0.467→0.474 but NLL didn't).\n\nThe reason sharpens the rule: because 94% of ordinal *training* questions collided, the head **learned that the lexical view is useless for this question type** and routes around it. The view gates are shared across types, so nothing makes it trusted again at inference. **Enrichment pays only where the head already relies on the channel being enriched** — true of Choice options and their keys, not true of ordinal options.\n\nI've written this up as the clearest remaining lead (fix it in *training*, not serving) rather than attempting it, because the evidence doesn't justify another full retrain on its own.\n\n## Also\n\nI hit two more of my own silent-failure patterns this round — running from the wrong directory, and `2>&1` merging stderr into a JSON stream. Both now route stderr to a file so errors surface instead of producing empty or unparseable output.\n\n## State\n\n`/workspace/candidate` holds the 0.28955 artifact, untouched by any probe — `validate-candidate` clean, 512.5M params, 2.05 GiB peak, stress suite passing, re-confirmed by the Judge. `NOTES.md` + `runs.md` now document ~25 experiments across 111 table rows, every negative result with the number that killed it, and the harness bug classes with their structural fixes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":563,"cache_read_input_tokens":709448,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":563},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5e37b52e-1e5b-4ee1-bd03-e7d0043bc94c","uuid":"6708569b-f9a9-41b6-9f78-ebd46dcd49ff","request_id":"req_011CfKiLPkDTo1wtLjrpkrku"}
