{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfKkiPLGbJC8QH6eqJdij","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VN8bg9jsqRkrkvMAvTR4n7","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> runs.md <<'EOF'\n\n### Training with indexed ordinal levels: the hypothesis refuted at its core\nServing with indexed levels was neutral, and the explanation offered was that the head had learned\nto ignore the lexical view on ordinal questions, so the fix had to go into training. Both members\nwere retrained with `--score_style indexed` (only that flag changed; option rendering held at the\nshipped train-`desc`/serve-`key_desc`).\n\nResult: **0.2888 against 0.2924**, and — the decisive part — *the ordinal sources got worse*:\nlegacy_holdout +0.021, unknowable_control +0.013, ordinal_mae +0.027. Knowledge also fell\n(+0.019). Only emotion improved (-0.029), and it has no ordinal questions.\n\nSo the defect was real (94% first-token [REDACTED] but the diagnosis was wrong. A level index is\nperfectly correlated with option *position*, and position is already available to the head through\nthe letter view and the learned slot prior. Adding it inside the option span does not give the\nmodel information it lacked; it gives it a second copy of information it already had, in a channel\nthat then competes with reading the level *description*. The head takes the shortcut and content\nlearning is displaced — the same failure mode as the lexical view crowding out the pointer view\nearly in this project.\n\nWorth stating plainly: this was my own hypothesis, argued from a measured defect, and the\nexperiment refuted it on exactly the questions it was designed to fix.\nEOF\n/opt/kev-venv/bin/python -c \"\nimport torch;h=torch.load('/workspace/candidate/checkpoint/head.pt',map_location='cpu',weights_only=True)\nprint('candidate unchanged:', h['letter_style'], h['pointer_style'], 'score_style=', h.get('score_style','(absent->plain)'))\"\nvalidate-candidate --json | head -2\n/opt/kev-venv/bin/python /opt/kev-runtime/evaluate_public.py --candidate /workspace/candidate 2>/tmp/e.err > /tmp/e.json && /opt/kev-venv/bin/python -c \"\nimport json;m=json.load(open('/tmp/e.json'))['metrics'];print('candidate dev=%.4f (Judge 0.28955)'%m['reward'])\"","description":"Record the refutation and verify the candidate","timeout":2400000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1162,"cache_read_input_tokens":717383,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1162},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5e37b52e-1e5b-4ee1-bd03-e7d0043bc94c","uuid":"3f9bd4bc-9fd2-40ee-8415-d76eb3c4345e","request_id":"req_011CfKkiLhG7Z5e3vPpQoM5V"}
