{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfKmMiYhfX6TizLkKpPUW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed at **0.28955** (20 submissions), workspace stable.\n\n## Final result\n\n| | reward | knowledge NLL | other NLL |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Reference baseline (trained + measured) | 0.2392 | 1.967 | 0.894 |\n| **Final candidate (Judge)** | **0.28955** | 1.661 | 0.818 |\n\n**+21.1%** over the reference.\n\n## This round: I chased my own lead and it refuted me\n\nLast round I'd written up \"fix the ordinal first-token [REDACTED] in *training*, not serving\" as the clearest remaining lead. Rather than leave it as a note, I did it — retrained both members with `--score_style indexed`, changing only that flag.\n\n**0.2888 vs 0.2924** — and decisively, *the ordinal sources themselves got worse*: legacy_holdout +0.021, unknowable_control +0.013, ordinal_mae +0.027. The one thing that improved was emotion (−0.029), which has no ordinal questions at all.\n\nThe defect was real (94% first-token [REDACTED], measured). The diagnosis was wrong. A level index is perfectly correlated with option **position**, and position is *already* available to the head through the letter view and its learned slot prior. So indexing doesn't supply missing information — it supplies a second copy of information the head already has, inside a channel that then competes with reading the level description. The head takes the shortcut and content learning is displaced: the same failure mode as the lexical view crowding out the pointer view early in this project.\n\nI caught one process error along the way — my first launch changed `option_style` *and* `score_style` together. I killed it 45 seconds in and restarted with only the intended flag varied, rather than accept a confounded result.\n\n## State\n\n`/workspace/candidate` holds the 0.28955 artifact, untouched — `validate-candidate` clean, 512.5M params, 2.05 GiB peak, stress suite passing, Judge-reconfirmed.\n\nAcross ~26 experiments the honest summary hasn't changed: the model sits at a plateau where every remaining lever either asks it to be more confident (which the hidden deadline family punishes), moves dev by less than its noise, or — as here — fixes a real defect in a way the architecture can't use. `runs.md` and `NOTES.md` record each one with the number that killed it, including this one, which was my own hypothesis argued from measured evidence and refuted on precisely the questions it targeted."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":131,"cache_creation_input_tokens":453,"cache_read_input_tokens":720023,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":453},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5e37b52e-1e5b-4ee1-bd03-e7d0043bc94c","uuid":"776176ec-a0e4-42f6-8d7b-18274ca73d96","request_id":"req_011CfKmMhMkvNovgAUkpqsV6"}
