{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfKmmMiV5gEy6hCJ4eUmX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This round I verified the deployment path rather than the model — the other way a submission fails.\n\n## Final result\n\n| | reward | knowledge NLL | other NLL |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Reference baseline (trained + measured) | 0.2392 | 1.967 | 0.894 |\n| **Final candidate (Judge, best of 20)** | **0.28955** | 1.661 | 0.818 |\n\n**+21.0%** over the reference.\n\n## Deployment verification\n\nI'd been checking budgets from my own harness, running as root from the experiments directory — which is not how the Judge runs. `judge_sim.py` reproduces the worker properly: clean interpreter, unrelated working directory (`/tmp`), only the candidate on `sys.path`, one visible GPU, `HOME=/tmp`, requests fed one at a time — and executed **as an unprivileged user (uid 1000)**, which is how the Judge loads the checkpoint.\n\n| budget | limit | measured |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| model load | 180 s | 11.6 s |\n| slowest single request | 45 s | 0.60 s |\n| whole worker (load + 2,068 questions) | 20 min | 3.2 min |\n| peak Torch allocation | 16 GiB | 2.05 GiB |\n| valid predictions | all | 1156 / 1156 |\n\nI also verified world-readability by **actually reading the files as that user** rather than inspecting mode bits, and confirmed there are no `__pycache__` or stray `.pyc` files that could shadow an import. Test user removed afterwards.\n\n## Trajectory\n\nThe 20 submissions show where the gains came from: calibration (0.2826→0.2839), training the pointer member I'd left at reference defaults (→0.2882), and the serving-time option-key discovery that came out of a harness bug (→0.28955). Knowledge moved 1.681→1.661; \"other\" moved 0.846→0.818. Four submissions went *down* — each one a hypothesis dev supported and the hidden set rejected, and each is written up with the number that killed it.\n\nThe model has been at a plateau for the last several rounds: every remaining lever either asks it to be more confident (punished by the hidden deadline family), moves dev by less than its noise, or fixes a real defect the architecture can't use. What I've added since is verification depth rather than score."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":941,"cache_read_input_tokens":727979,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":941},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5e37b52e-1e5b-4ee1-bd03-e7d0043bc94c","uuid":"1dfffd47-8480-46b4-987a-bf519fe4a952","request_id":"req_011CfKmmMAF7549eR81G5TxU"}
